दक्ष् द॑क्षति द॑क्ष˚ते A. satisfy, please (dat.);
 M.
be able or strong. C. दक्ष॑यति make able or strong.

द॑क्ष a. able, capable, appropriate, suitable, fit for,
clever in (loc. or —˚);
 strong, mighty;
 intelligent, wise, right (not
left). m. ability, power, fitness, cleverness, intelligence, energy,
will, disposition, (evil) design;
 N. of an Aditya, also identif. w.
Prajāpati.

द॑क्षिण a. able, capable of, fit for (—˚);
 right (not
left), southern;
 upright, honest;
 amiable, polite, chivalrous.
दक्षिणं w. परि-इ walk round a person with the right side towards
him;
 w. कृ = दक्षिणतःकृ q.v. —m. the right hand or arm, the right
hand horse;
 the right side, the south (m. or n.). f. आ (scil. गो) a
good milch-cow;
 a present given to officiating priests (orig. a cow);
fee, donation, gift i.g.;
 (±दिश्) the south.

दक्षिण॑ a. able, capable of, fit for (—˚);
 right (not
left), southern;
 upright, honest;
 amiable, polite, chivalrous.
दक्षिणं w. परि-इ walk round a person with the right side towards
him;
 w. कृ = दक्षिणतःकृ q.v. —m. the right hand or arm, the right
hand horse;
 the right side, the south (m. or n.). f. आ (scil. गो) a
good milch-cow;
 a present given to officiating priests (orig. a cow);
fee, donation, gift i.g.;
 (±दिश्) the south.

दक्षिणामुख a. turning the face to the right or to
the south;
 n. adv.

द॑क्षिणावन्त् a. able, fit;
 rich in offerings or
presents, pious.

दाक्षिण्य = दाक्षिण॑;
 n. civility, kindness, gallantry
towards (loc., gen., or —˚);
 the south.

दाक्षिणात्य a. southerly, belonging to the Dekhan;
 m. or
n. the south, m. pl. the inhabitants of the Dekhan.
